Z||000000||billfredmike24||06-16-2000||04:31 PM||||Got the oil changed and was told i had cracked rear outer c.v. boot<BR>GM dealer said about $175 to fix.<BR>Local garage said $172.50, they said they had to take the back axle off to fix it.<BR>If prices are so close im thinking that the dealer will be doing some other procedure.  I've read about a split boot?, would this result in not talking off axle?<BR>any suggestions would be helpful<BR>TIA||||reg||5
Z||000001||Gold-86SE||06-16-2000||04:44 PM||||<BR>Every time that I had my cv joints repaired, I pulled the shaft from the tranny and took the half shaft the shop were they rebuilt the cv joints.  My cost was generally under $100.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Gokart||06-16-2000||08:26 PM||||I have a nail size hole in mine and it was shooting small amounts of grease at the oil pan. Six months back I bought a plastic injection type thingy filled with axle grease, filled it back up then covered the hole with a small piece of duct tape! Hasn't leaked since <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||olympic||06-16-2000||09:15 PM||||  Be careful, I don't think that your suppose to use plain old axle grease on CV joints....  As far as the split boots go, you dont have to remove the axle to install them.  I've never tried them but I've heard that in warm climates they work quite well.  Try them out but keep an eye on them.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Mark||06-17-2000||09:16 AM||||I have used the split boots in the past and they do work pretty well.  I would recommend the "screw-together" type (the boot has a small flange at the joint and screws and nuts are used to fasten the split together).  The other type of split boot, which I do not prefer, uses glue (it's difficult to keep the glue surfaces clean).<P>I would think that either version would work well on a fiero since the boot doesn't have to flex as much as in a FWD installation.<P>Just remember to clean the CV joint thoroughly and repack it with the grease provided in the CV joint boot kit.||||reg||1
